{"userInfo":{"institute":false,"member":false,"individual":false,"guest":false,"subscribedContent":false,"fileCabinetContent":false,"fileCabinetUser":false,"dtrDeleteCookieOnLogout":false,"institutionalFileCabinetUser":false,"dtrCookieExpirationDays":0,"showPatentCitations":true,"showGet802Link":false,"showOpenUrlLink":false,"tracked":false,"institutionUserId":0,"delegatedAdmin":false,"desktop":false,"isInstitutionDashboardEnabled":false,"isInstitutionProfileEnabled":false,"isRoamingEnabled":false,"isDelegatedAdmin":false,"isMdl":false,"isCwg":false,"isReadAndPublish":false,"isIel":false,"isAcademic":false},"figures":[{"id":"fig1","label":"Fig. 1.","graphic":{"href":"song1-3700605.eps","small":"song1-3700605-small.gif","orientation":"portrait","large":"song1-3700605-large.gif","hires":"song1-3700605-hires.gif","glance":"song1-3700605-glance.gif","position":"float"},"caption":"<p>Order-driven scheduling strategy considers each task as a discrete order and decomposes the EOSTSP as a three-stage process, achieving the online scheduling; TSLC framework employs distinct LLM-based agents making decisions at three stages while the PM and CV verify the solution feasibility, achieving the autonomous scheduling.</p>","orientation":"portrait","part":"1","position":"float"},{"id":"fig2","label":"Fig. 2.","graphic":{"href":"song2-3700605.eps","small":"song2-3700605-small.gif","orientation":"portrait","large":"song2-3700605-large.gif","hires":"song2-3700605-hires.gif","glance":"song2-3700605-glance.gif","position":"float"},"caption":"<p>Order-driven scheduling strategy; for each order-driven task, AS assigns the satellite, VS selects the VTW, ES determines the observation time; each decision should be verified by the scheduled tasks and occupied satellite, and influences the overall scheduling plan.</p>","orientation":"portrait","part":"1","position":"float"},{"id":"fig3","label":"Fig. 3.","graphic":{"href":"song3-3700605.eps","small":"song3-3700605-small.gif","orientation":"portrait","large":"song3-3700605-large.gif","hires":"song3-3700605-hires.gif","glance":"song3-3700605-glance.gif","position":"float"},"caption":"<p>Workflow of the TSLC framework; the AS, VS, and ES make sequential decisions to complete the scheduled plan; the MS and CV guide the PM to evaluate the decision and subsequent optimization.</p>","orientation":"portrait","part":"1","position":"float"},{"id":"fig4","label":"Fig. 4.","graphic":{"href":"song4-3700605.eps","small":"song4-3700605-small.gif","orientation":"portrait","large":"song4-3700605-large.gif","hires":"song4-3700605-hires.gif","glance":"song4-3700605-glance.gif","position":"float"},"caption":"<p>Prompts for each agent; every prompt describes the name, ability, and responsibilities during the tri-stage process.</p>","orientation":"portrait","part":"1","position":"float"},{"id":"fig5","label":"Fig. 5.","graphic":{"href":"song5-3700605.eps","small":"song5-3700605-small.gif","orientation":"portrait","large":"song5-3700605-large.gif","hires":"song5-3700605-hires.gif","glance":"song5-3700605-glance.gif","position":"float"},"caption":"<p>Geographic distribution of mission target points from the “Tian Zhi Bei” dataset, illustrating the high concentration over terrestrial regions and the formation of high-demand “hotspots.”</p>","orientation":"portrait","part":"1","position":"float"},{"id":"fig6","label":"Fig. 6.","graphic":{"href":"song6-3700605.eps","small":"song6-3700605-small.gif","orientation":"portrait","large":"song6-3700605-large.gif","hires":"song6-3700605-hires.gif","glance":"song6-3700605-glance.gif","position":"float"},"caption":"<p>AS, VS, and ES makes the scheduling decisions while the PM check its feasibility; The CV and information of real-time scenario support the verification with the staged constraint checking, where the PM iteratively validates each agent’s decision, and this process updates the MS <inline-formula>\n    <tex-math notation=\"LaTeX\">\\${\\mathcal {MS}}\\$</tex-math>\n  </inline-formula> with failed attempts and the knowledge base <inline-formula>\n    <tex-math notation=\"LaTeX\">\\${\\mathcal {K}}\\$</tex-math>\n  </inline-formula> with the final confirmed schedule.</p>","orientation":"portrait","part":"1","position":"float"},{"id":"fig7","label":"Fig. 7.","graphic":{"href":"song7-3700605.eps","small":"song7-3700605-small.gif","orientation":"portrait","large":"song7-3700605-large.gif","hires":"song7-3700605-hires.gif","glance":"song7-3700605-glance.gif","position":"float"},"caption":"<p>Consumed tokens per chat for all routine scenarios at three scheduling stages.</p>","orientation":"portrait","part":"1","position":"float"},{"id":"fig8","label":"Fig. 8.","graphic":{"href":"song8-3700605.eps","small":"song8-3700605-small.gif","orientation":"portrait","large":"song8-3700605-large.gif","hires":"song8-3700605-hires.gif","glance":"song8-3700605-glance.gif","position":"float"},"caption":"<p>Consumed tokens per task for all routine scenarios at three scheduling stages.</p>","orientation":"portrait","part":"1","position":"float"},{"id":"fig9","label":"Fig. 9.","graphic":{"href":"song9-3700605.eps","small":"song9-3700605-small.gif","orientation":"portrait","large":"song9-3700605-large.gif","hires":"song9-3700605-hires.gif","glance":"song9-3700605-glance.gif","position":"float"},"caption":"<p>Cumulative atomic chats at each phase across different scenarios.</p>","orientation":"portrait","part":"1","position":"float"},{"id":"fig10","label":"Fig. 10.","graphic":{"href":"song10-3700605.eps","small":"song10-3700605-small.gif","orientation":"portrait","large":"song10-3700605-large.gif","hires":"song10-3700605-hires.gif","glance":"song10-3700605-glance.gif","position":"float"},"caption":"<p>Atomic chats for individual tasks at each phase across different scenarios.</p>","orientation":"portrait","part":"1","position":"float"},{"id":"fig11","label":"Fig. 11.","graphic":{"href":"song11-3700605.eps","small":"song11-3700605-small.gif","orientation":"portrait","large":"song11-3700605-large.gif","hires":"song11-3700605-hires.gif","glance":"song11-3700605-glance.gif","position":"float"},"caption":"<p>Total and successful atomic chats generated by TSLC with different LLMs or without prompt modules on scenario 80-540. Red numbers indicate the percentage of successful scheduling chats among all atomic chats.</p>","orientation":"portrait","part":"1","position":"float"}],"articleNumber":"11552394","mediaPath":"/mediastore/IEEE/content/media/36/11333908/11552394","getProgramTermsAccepted":false,"formulaStrippedArticleTitle":"A Tri-Stage LLM-Coordinated Framework for Order-Driven Scheduling of Earth Observation Satellite Tasks","pubLink":"/xpl/RecentIssue.jsp?punumber=36","allowComments":false,"issueLink":"/xpl/tocresult.jsp?isnumber=null&punumber=36","isGetAddressInfoCaptured":false,"isMarketingOptIn":false,"publisher":"IEEE","displayDocTitle":"A Tri-Stage LLM-Coordinated Framework for Order-Driven Scheduling of Earth Observation Satellite Tasks","isEarlyAccess":false,"isOpenAccess":false,"isEphemera":false,"isConference":false,"isPromo":false,"isTutorial":false,"isChapter":false,"isOnlineOnly":false,"isBook":false,"isStandard":false,"isProduct":false,"isJournal":true,"isFreeDocument":false,"isDynamicHtml":false,"isSpringer":false,"isBookWithoutChapters":false,"xploreDocumentType":"Journals & Magazine","isLatestStandard":false,"hasStandardVersions":false,"isGiveaway":false,"isTranslation":false,"isCustomDenial":false,"persistentLink":"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/servlet/opac?punumber=36","isSMPTE":false,"isOUP":false,"isSAE":false,"isNow":false,"isDegruyter":false,"htmlAbstractLink":"/document/11552394/","contentTypeDisplay":"Journals","mlTime":"PT0.028059S","lastupdate":"2026-10-04","mediaPath":"/mediastore/IEEE/content/media/36/11333908/11552394","title":"A Tri-Stage LLM-Coordinated Framework for Order-Driven Scheduling of Earth Observation Satellite Tasks","contentType":"periodicals","publicationNumber":"36"}